          <h1 id="journey-title">Turning satellite data into useful decisions.</h1>
          <p>I work where Earth observation, geospatial AI and product development meet—helping teams move from technical capability to services people can understand, trust and use.</p>
          <div class="button-row">
            <a class="button" href="/about/">Explore my profile</a>
            <a class="button ghost" href="/writing/">Read my writing</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="story-panel" data-story="1">
          <p class="mission-code">01 · LIFTOFF</p>
          <h2>Start with the problem, not the platform.</h2>
          <p>Satellite data can reveal extraordinary things, but technical sophistication alone does not create value. The journey begins with the user need and the decision the system should support.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="story-panel" data-story="2">
          <p class="mission-code">02 · STAGING</p>
          <h2>Separate complexity into the right layers.</h2>
          <p>Reliable services emerge when infrastructure, data, models and delivery responsibilities are clearly separated—then deliberately connected around a shared outcome.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="story-panel" data-story="3">
          <p class="mission-code">03 · DEPLOYMENT</p>
          <h2>Translate capability into an experience people can use.</h2>
          <p>My work bridges geospatial workflows, product direction, partner coordination and AI-assisted interaction so that the final insight remains understandable and trustworthy.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="story-panel story-final" data-story="4">
          <p class="mission-code">04 · ORBIT</p>
          <h2>Build systems that remain useful after launch.</h2>
          <p>I combine Earth-observation domain knowledge, technical programme leadership and product thinking to help promising capabilities become dependable services.</p>
          <div class="button-row">
            <a class="button" href="/projects/">Explore my work</a>
            <a class="button ghost" href="/about/">Professional profile</a>
          </div>
        </article>
